ATC System Design: CRC Cards

--------------------------------------------------------
CRC Card
Class: TransponderReceiver
Responsibilities:
- Receive high-density data packets from aircraft transponders.
- Unpack flight data and aircraft type information.
- Send extracted data to the database for storage.

Collaborators (if any):
- AircraftDatabase.

Assumptions (if any):
- The receiver handles the conversion from high-density packet format to a readable data structure.
--------------------------------------------------------
CRC Card
Class: AircraftDatabase
Responsibilities:
- Store unpacked flight and aircraft information.
- Provide aircraft data for display updates and safety analysis.
- Search for specific aircraft details based on controller queries.

Collaborators (if any):
- None.

Assumptions (if any):
- The database is maintained in memory for fast 10-second updates.
--------------------------------------------------------
CRC Card
Class: SafetyAnalyzer
Responsibilities:
- Analyze stored aircraft data for dangerous proximity or paths.
- Detect dangerous flight situations.
- Signal alerts when a conflict is identified.

Collaborators (if any):
- AircraftDatabase.

Assumptions (if any):
- "Dangerous situations" are defined by the system's proximity logic.
--------------------------------------------------------
CRC Card
Class: DisplayController
Responsibilities:
- Build a graphical representation of aircraft from the database.
- Update the graphics display every 10 seconds.
- Refresh on-screen information for the controller.

Collaborators (if any):
- AircraftDatabase.

Assumptions (if any):
- The system provides a 10-second timer to trigger the refresh.
--------------------------------------------------------
CRC Card
Class: QueryManager
Responsibilities:
- Receive and process database queries from the controller.
- Fetch specific plane details from the database based on screen selection.
- Return plane details to the controller interface.

Collaborators (if any):
- AircraftDatabase.

Assumptions (if any):
- The controller queries the database via an interface on the graphics screen.
--------------------------------------------------------
